The attached image displays flow cytometry histograms (Figure 6) demonstrating that Nano-11 enhances the expression of costimulatory molecules on dendritic cells (DCs). Bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) were incubated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) or medium control (gray line) for two days. The histograms show that Nano-11 treatment leads to a slight increase in CD40 expression, and a marked increase in the expression of both CD80 and CD86. This indicates that Nano-11 activates DCs in vitro, a crucial step for initiating an effective adaptive immune response.